#: ../../export/model_archive.rst:3
msgid "Marquetry Archive"
msgstr ""

#: ../../export/model_archive.rst:5
msgid ""
"The marquetry archive (recommended extension: ``.mq``) stores the traced "
"computation graph and the weights in one zip file, without any extra "
"dependency. Unlike :meth:`marquetry.Layer.save_params` (weights only), "
"the archive can be loaded back **without the original model class**, and "
"the restored model supports both inference and further training."
msgstr ""

#: marquetry.model_archive.serializer.save_archive:1 of
msgid "Save a model as a marquetry archive (graph + weights, ``.mq``)."
msgstr ""

#: marquetry.model_archive.serializer.save_archive:3 of
msgid ""
"Runs one forward pass with the sample inputs to record the computation "
"graph, then stores every traced function verbatim (class name and "
"constructor attributes) together with the parameters, so the archive can "
"be loaded and executed without the original model class."
msgstr ""

#: ../../export/model_archive.rst
msgid "Parameters"
msgstr ""

#: marquetry.model_archive.serializer.save_archive:8 of
msgid "The model to save."
msgstr ""

#: marquetry.model_archive.serializer.save_archive:10 of
msgid ""
"A sample input array (or :class:`marquetry.Container`), or a tuple/list "
"of them for multi-input models."
msgstr ""

#: marquetry.model_archive.serializer.save_archive:12 of
msgid "Destination path. ``.mq`` is the recommended extension."
msgstr ""

#: marquetry.model_archive.serializer.save_archive:14 of
msgid ""
"If True, reshape targets whose leading dim follows the batch axis are "
"stored as batch-relative so the loaded model accepts any batch size."
msgstr ""

#: marquetry.model_archive.loader.load_archive:1 of
msgid "Load a marquetry archive saved by :func:`save_archive`."
msgstr ""

#: marquetry.model_archive.loader.load_archive:3 of
msgid "Path to the archive file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../export/model_archive.rst
msgid "Returns"
msgstr ""

#: marquetry.model_archive.loader.load_archive:6 of
msgid ""
"A runnable model which replays the stored graph.     Its parameters are "
"trainable :class:`marquetry.Parameter` objects,     so the loaded model "
"supports both inference and further training."
msgstr ""

#: marquetry.model_archive.loader.load_archive:8 of
msgid "A runnable model which replays the stored graph."
msgstr ""

#: marquetry.model_archive.loader.load_archive:9 of
msgid ""
"Its parameters are trainable :class:`marquetry.Parameter` objects, so the"
" loaded model supports both inference and further training."
msgstr ""

#: ../../export/model_archive.rst
msgid "Return type"
msgstr ""

#: marquetry.model_archive.loader.GraphModel:1 of
msgid "A model reconstructed from a marquetry archive."
msgstr ""

#: marquetry.model_archive.loader.GraphModel:3 of
msgid ""
"The stored graph is replayed by re-applying the original "
":mod:`marquetry.functions` classes node by node, so the loaded model "
"behaves like the traced one: backpropagation, train/test mode dispatch "
"(dropout, batch normalization) and parameter updates all work."
msgstr ""

#: marquetry.model_archive.loader.GraphModel.forward:1 of
msgid ""
"Perform the forward computation of the layer. Subclasses must implement "
"this method."
msgstr ""

#: marquetry.model_archive.loader.GraphModel.forward:3 of
msgid "Input data arrays."
msgstr ""

#: marquetry.model_archive.loader.GraphModel.forward:6 of
msgid "Output data arrays."
msgstr ""

#: marquetry.model_archive.loader.GraphModel.forward:9 of
msgid ""
"Generally, this class shouldn't be called by manually because `forward` "
"is called by `__call__`."
msgstr ""

#: marquetry.model_archive.spec.ArchiveError:1 of
msgid "Raised when a model can't be saved to or loaded from a marquetry archive."
msgstr ""

